From: ROG5 Linux Project <rog5-linux@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: add timeout-safe, nonblocking RPMh read requests

Provide observation of inherited APPS resource votes without registering new
regulators, changing voltage/mode policy, or touching wake/sleep vote caches.
The read message encoding follows the Qualcomm rpmh_read proposal:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260801-b4-read-rpmh-v5-v6-1-9fcb54928523@oss.qualcomm.com/

Unlike the upstream on-stack read request, retain independent caller and IRQ
references. Timeout leaves the request alive until a late completion; no
caller-owned output pointer survives the call. Read slot admission is a single
attempt, returning EAGAIN if busy. Existing writer waiting/caching is unchanged.

Use the existing ten-second response wait. Existing finite MMIO synchronization
polls precede it; this is not a guarantee against a wedged processor or bus.
This adds only the read transport; regulator initial-state behavior is unchanged.

